verses.text:
Your country is desolate,
your cities are burned with fire;
your land, strangers devour it in your presence,
and it is desolate, as overthrown by strangers.{c}

Zion’s daughter remains like a lean-to in a vineyard,
like a watchman’s hut in a melon patch,
like a town under blockade.{d}

Unless Yahweh of Armies had left to us a small remnant,
we would have been as Sodom,
we would have been like Gomorrah.{e}

Hear the word of Yahweh,
you rulers of Sodom;
give ear to the law of our God,
you people of Gomorrah!{f}

Your new moons and your appointed feasts my soul hates;
they are a burden to me;
I am weary of bearing them.

And when you spread forth your hands,
I will hide my eyes from you;
yes, when you make many prayers, I will not hear;
your hands are full of blood.{g}

Wash yourselves, make yourselves clean;
put away the evil of your doings from before my eyes;
cease to do evil;

learn to do good;
seek justice, set right the oppressor;
judge the fatherless, plead for the widow.”{h}

“Come now, and let us reason together,” says Yahweh:
“Though your sins are as scarlet,
they shall be as white as snow;
though they are red like crimson,
they shall be as wool.{i}

but if you refuse and are rebellious,
by the sword you shall be eaten;
for the mouth of Yahweh has spoken.”

And I will bring my hand back upon you,
and refine your dross as with lye,
and will take away all your alloy.{k}

The strong person will become kindling,
his work a spark;
both will burn together,
and no one will put them out.{n}

And it shall come to pass in the latter days
that the mountain of the house of Yahweh
shall be established at the top of the mountains,
and shall be exalted above the hills;
and all the nations shall stream to it.{a}

He will settle disputes among the nations
and arbitrate for many peoples;
they will hammer their swords into plowshares
and their spears into pruning knives;
one nation will not raise a sword against another,
and they will never train for war again.

Their land also is full of idols;
they worship the work of their own hands,
that which their own fingers have made.{d}

And man is bowed down,
and each one is brought low;
and do not forgive them!{e}

Enter into the rock,
and hide in the dust,
from before the terror of Yahweh,
and from the splendor of his majesty.{f}

For Yahweh of Armies has a day
against all that is proud and lofty,
and against all that is lifted up, and it shall be brought low;

and against all the cedars of Lebanon,
that are high and lifted up,
and against all the oaks of Bashan;{g}

And the loftiness of man shall be bowed down,
and the haughtiness of men shall be brought low;
and Yahweh alone shall be exalted in that day.

in that day he shall lift up his voice, saying,
“I will not be a binder of wounds;
for in my house is neither bread nor cloak;
you shall not make me ruler of the people.”

For Jerusalem has stumbled, and Judah has fallen,
because their tongue and their doings are against Yahweh,
to defy the eyes of his glory.{c}

therefore the Lord will afflict with scabs
the heads of Zion’s daughters,
and Yahweh will lay bare their secret parts.”{g}

Then instead of perfume there will be a stench;
instead of a sash, a rope;
instead of styled hair, baldness;
instead of fine clothing, sackcloth;
and a brand instead of beauty.{i}

And seven women shall take hold of one man in that day, saying,
“We will eat our own bread and wear our own clothing;
only let us be called by your name;
take away our reproach.”

He dug it up and gathered out its stones,
and planted it with the finest vine,
and built a tower in the midst of it,
and also hewed out a winepress in it;
and he looked for it to yield grapes,
and it yielded wild grapes.{b}

I will turn it into a ruin;
no one will prune or hoe it,
but briers and thorns will take over;
I will also command the clouds
not to send rain on it.”

For the vineyard of Yahweh of Armies is the house of Israel,
and the men of Judah his pleasant planting;
and he looked for justice, but behold, bloodshed;
for righteousness, but behold, a cry!{c}

In my ears Yahweh of Armies has sworn:
“Surely many houses shall be desolate,
great and fair, without inhabitant.{d}

And the lyre and the harp, the tambourine and the flute, and wine are at their feasts;
but they do not regard the work of Yahweh,
nor see the deeds of his hands.

Therefore my people go into exile for lack of knowledge;
and their honored men are famished,
and their multitude is parched with thirst.

Therefore Sheol has enlarged her appetite,
and opened her mouth without measure;
and their glory and their multitude and their tumult go down into it,
and he who exults among them.{f}

Woe to those who call evil good, and good evil;
who put darkness for light, and light for darkness;
who put bitter for sweet, and sweet for bitter!

Therefore the anger of Yahweh is kindled against his people,
and he has stretched out his hand against them and struck them;
and the mountains trembled,
and their dead bodies became like refuse in the streets.
For all this his anger has not turned back,
but his hand is stretched out still.{i}

And he will lift up a banner to the nations from far away,
and will whistle for them from the end of the earth;
and behold, they shall come with speed, swiftly.

None shall be weary nor stumble among them;
none shall slumber nor sleep;
neither shall the girdle of their loins be loosed,
nor the thong of their sandals be broken;

And they shall growl over it in that day
like the roaring of the sea;
and if one gazes at the land,
behold, darkness, distress;
even the light grows dark in its clouds.

And one called to another and said:
“Holy, holy, holy is Yahweh of Armies;
the whole earth is full of his glory!”{c}

And he said, “Go, and say to this people:
‘Hear indeed, but do not understand;
and see indeed, but do not perceive.’

thus says the Lord Yahweh:
“It shall not stand,
neither shall it come to pass.{e}

Therefore the Lord himself will give you a sign:
Behold, the young woman shall conceive and bear a son,
and shall call his name Immanuel.{i}

“Because this people has refused
the waters of Shiloah that go softly,
and rejoices in Rezin and the son of Remaliah;{d}

now therefore, behold, the Lord brings up upon them
the waters of the River, strong and many,
the king of Assyria and all his glory;
and it shall come up over all its channels,
and go over all its banks;

and it shall sweep on into Judah;
it shall overflow and pass through;
it shall reach even to the neck;
and the spreading of its wings shall fill the breadth of your land,
O Immanuel.”{e}

Be broken, O peoples, and be shattered;
give ear, all you of far countries;
gird yourselves, and be shattered;
gird yourselves, and be shattered.{f}

Take counsel together, and it shall come to nothing;
speak the word, and it shall not stand;
for God is with us.{g}

“Do not call conspiracy
all that this people calls conspiracy;
neither fear what they fear,
nor be in dread.{i}

Yahweh of Armies, him shall you regard as holy;
he is the one for you to fear,
he is the one for you to dread.

And he shall become a holy place;
but a stone to strike against and a rock to trip over
for the two houses of Israel,
a trap and a snare
to the inhabitants of Jerusalem.{j}

People who walked in the dark have seen a great light.
For the inhabitants of a land of gloomy shadow,
light has begun to shine.{b}

You have made the nation larger
and increased its happiness;
they celebrate in your presence as people do at harvest,
as they shout with joy when dividing plunder.{c}

A child is born to us, and a son is given to us;
authority is on his shoulder,
and his name will be
Wonderful Counselor, Mighty God,
Eternal Father, Prince of Peace.{e}

“Bricks have fallen down,
but with hewn stone we will build;
sycamores are felled,
but cedars we will set in their stead.”{h}

Syria in front and the Philistines behind;
and they eat up Israel with gaping mouth.
For all this his anger has not turned back,
and his hand is stretched out still.{i}

So the Lord takes no pleasure in their young men
and shows no pity to their orphans and widows,
for all of them are ungodly and do evil,
and every mouth utters nonsense.
Despite all this, his anger has not turned away,
and his hand is still raised.{k}

Wickedness blazes like a fire that devours thorns and briers;
it ignites the dense forest,
and the smoke swirls upward in a column.

Through the wrath of Yahweh of Armies the land is scorched,
and the people are like food for the fire;
no man spares his brother.{l}

They slice meat on the right, and are still hungry;
they eat on the left, and are not satisfied;
each devours the flesh of his own arm,{m}

Is Calno not as Carchemish?
Is Hamath not as Arpad?
Is Samaria not as Damascus?{d}

For he says:
“By the strength of my hand I have done it,
and by my wisdom, for I have understanding;
I have removed the borders of peoples,
and plundered their treasures;
and like a mighty one I have brought down those who sat on thrones.{f}

My hand has found the riches of the peoples
as one finds a nest;
and as men gather abandoned eggs,
so I have gathered all the earth;
and there was none that moved a wing,
or opened a mouth, or chirped.”

Therefore the Lord, Yahweh of Armies,
will send wasting sickness among his fat ones;
and under his glory a burning shall be kindled,
like the burning of fire.{h}

And the glory of his forest and of his fruitful field
he will consume, both soul and body;
and it shall be as when a sick man wastes away.{i}

He has come to Aiath;
he has passed through Migron;
at Michmash he stores his baggage.{p}

They have gone across the ravine;
“Geba shall be our lodging,” they say;
Ramah is afraid;
Saul’s Gibeah is fleeing.{q}

Cry aloud with your voice, O daughter of Gallim!
Listen, O Laishah!
Answer her, O poor Anathoth!{r}

Yet today he will stand at Nob;
he waves his hand against the mountain of the daughter of Zion,
the hill of Jerusalem.{t}

His delight will be the fear of Yahweh.
He will not give a verdict based on what his eyes see
or settle a case by what his ears hear;

but he will judge the poor with righteousness
and give fair rulings for the humble in the land;
he will hit the earth with the rod of his mouth,
and kill the wicked with the breath from his lips.{c}

And the wolf shall dwell with the lamb,
and the leopard shall lie down with the young goat,
and the calf and the young lion and the fatling together;
and a little child shall lead them.{d}

They shall not hurt nor destroy
in all my holy mountain;
for the earth shall be full of the knowledge of Yahweh,
as the waters cover the sea.

But they shall swoop down upon the shoulder of the Philistines on the west;
together they shall despoil the sons of the east;
Edom and Moab shall be the reach of their hand,
and the children of Ammon shall obey them.{g}

Yahweh will completely dry up the gulf of the Egyptian sea;
he will wave his hand over the River with his scorching wind
and split it into seven streams,
so that people can walk across in sandals.{h}

And you shall say in that day:
“I will give thanks to you, Yahweh,
for though you were angry with me,
your anger turned away,
and you comfort me.{a}

Behold, God is my salvation;
I will trust, and will not be afraid;
for Yah, Yahweh, is my strength and my song,
and he has become my salvation.”{b}

And you shall say in that day:
“Give thanks to Yahweh, call on his name;
declare among the peoples what he has done;
make mention that his name is lifted high.

Raise a signal flag on a bare hilltop;
call out to them;
wave your hand so they will go through the gates of the nobles.

I myself have commanded my consecrated ones;
yes, I have called my mighty men for my anger,
my proudly exulting ones.{b}

They come from a far country,
from the end of the heavens,
Yahweh and the weapons of his indignation,
to destroy the whole land.{c}

and they shall be terrified.
Pangs and pains shall seize them;
they shall writhe like a woman in labor;
they shall look aghast at one another;
their faces shall be faces of flame.

For the stars of the heavens and their constellations
shall not give their light;
the sun shall be dark at its rising,
and the moon shall not shed its light.{e}

Their infants also shall be dashed to pieces before their eyes;
their houses shall be plundered,
and their wives ravished.{g}

Behold, I will stir up the Medes against them,
who will not value silver,
and take no delight in gold.{h}

And their bows shall shatter the young men;
and they shall have no pity on the fruit of the womb;
their eye shall not spare children.

Babylon, the most glorious of kingdoms,
the splendor and boast of the Chaldeans,
will end up like Sodom and Gomorrah, which God overturned.{i}

But desert creatures shall lie down there,
and their houses shall be full of howling beasts;
and ostriches shall dwell there,
and wild goats shall dance there.{j}

And hyenas shall cry in its towers,
and jackals in the palaces of pleasure;
and its time is near to come,
and its days shall not be prolonged.{k}

that you shall take up this taunt against the king of Babylon, and say:
“How the oppressor has ceased,
the insolent fury ceased!{c}

Sheol beneath is stirred up for you,
to meet you at your coming;
it rouses the shades for you,
all the leaders of the earth;
it makes rise from their thrones
all the kings of the nations.{d}

But you said in your heart,
‘Into heaven I will go up;
higher than the stars of God
I will raise my throne;
and I will sit on the mount of assembly
in the far reaches of the north;{f}

All the kings of the nations,
every one of them, rest in honor,
each in his own tomb;

Make ready a slaughter for his children
for the guilt of their fathers,
that they not rise up and take the earth,
nor fill the surface of the world with cities.”{i}

to break Assyria in my land,
and on my mountains to trample him under foot;
and his yoke shall depart from them,
and his burden depart from their shoulder.”{l}

Do not celebrate, all you Philistines,
because the rod that beat you is broken;
for from the snake’s root will come a viper,
and its offspring will be a flying fiery serpent.{n}

And the firstborn of the poor shall feed,
and the needy shall lie down in safety;
but I will kill your root with famine,
and your remnant shall be slain.{o}

The oracle concerning Moab.
Because in a night Ar of Moab is laid waste,
Moab is undone;
because in a night Kir of Moab is laid waste,
Moab is undone.{a}

People go up to the temple, and Dibon goes to its hilltop shrines, to weep;
Moab wails over Nebo and over Medeba;
every head is shaved bald,
and every beard is cut off.{b}

In their streets they gird themselves with sackcloth;
on their housetops and in their squares
every one wails, going down in weeping.

And Heshbon cries out, and Elealeh;
their voice is heard as far as Jahaz;
therefore the armed men of Moab cry aloud;
his soul trembles within him.{c}

My heart cries out for Moab;
her fugitives flee as far as Zoar and Eglath-shelishiyah;
the slope of Luhith is climbed in tears,
and along the road to Horonaim
they raise a cry of devastation.{d}

For the waters of Nimrim are desolate;
for the grass is withered, the new growth fails,
there is no green thing.{e}

So the wealth they have gotten,
and their stored-up goods,
they bear off across the Brook of the Willows.{f}

For the cry has gone around the border of Moab;
its wailing reaches to Eglaim,
and its wailing to Beer-elim.{g}

Send lambs as tribute to the ruler of the country,
from Sela, through the desert,
to the mountain of Zion’s daughter.{a}

“Give counsel, render a decision;
make your shadow as the night
in the midst of the noonday;
conceal the banished;
do not reveal the wanderer.

Let my outcasts sojourn with you;
as for Moab, be a refuge to them from the destroyer.”
When the oppressor has come to an end,
destruction has ceased,
and he who tramples under foot is consumed out of the land,{c}

We have heard about Moab’s pride—
how extremely proud he is—
his conceit, his pride and his rage;
his empty boasts are false.{e}

Therefore let Moab wail for Moab,
let every one wail;
for the raisin cakes of Kir-hareseth
you shall moan, utterly stricken.{f}

For the fields of Heshbon languish,
the vine of Sibmah;
the lords of the nations have struck down its choice branches,
which reached to Jazer,
which strayed into the wilderness;
its shoots spread out,
they crossed over the sea.{g}

Therefore I weep with the weeping of Jazer
for the vine of Sibmah;
I drench you with my tears,
O Heshbon and Elealeh;
for upon your summer fruit and upon your harvest
the shout has fallen.{h}

Gladness and joy have been removed from the orchards;
no one sings or shouts in the vineyards;
no one treads out wine in the presses;
I have ended the shouting.

The oracle concerning Damascus.
Behold, Damascus shall cease to be a city,
and shall become a heap of ruins.{a}

The cities of Aroer are forsaken;
they shall be for flocks,
which shall lie down, and none shall make them afraid.{b}

The fortress shall cease from Ephraim,
and the kingdom from Damascus;
and the remnant of Syria
shall be like the glory of the children of Israel,
says Yahweh of Armies.{c}

It will be like a reaper gathering the standing grain
and cutting the heads with his arm;
it will be like someone gathering leftover heads
in the Valley of Rephaim.{d}

In that day their fortified cities shall be
as the forsaken places of the woods and the mountaintops,
that were forsaken before the children of Israel;
and it shall be a waste.{f}

For you have forgotten the God of your salvation,
and have not remembered the Rock of your stronghold;
therefore you plant pleasant plants,
and set out slips of a foreign god;{g}

At that time a gift shall be brought to Yahweh of Armies
from a people drawn out and polished,
from a people dreaded from their beginning onward,
a nation of strength upon strength and of trampling down,
whose land the rivers divide,
to the place of the name of Yahweh of Armies, Mount Zion.{d}

A message about Egypt.
Look, Yahweh is riding on a fast cloud
and coming to Egypt;
the idols of Egypt will shake before him,
and the heart of Egypt will melt inside it.{a}

And the spirit of Egypt within it shall be emptied out,
and I will confound its counsel;
and they shall seek the idols and the charmers,
and the mediums and the spiritists.{b}

And I will give over the Egyptians
into the hand of a harsh master;
and a fierce king shall rule over them,”
says the Lord, Yahweh of Armies.{c}

and the canals shall stink,
and the streams of Egypt shall dwindle and dry up;
reeds and rushes shall wither.{d}

The bare places by the Nile, by the mouth of the Nile,
and every sown field of the Nile,
shall dry up, be driven away, and be no more.{e}

The princes of Zoan are utter fools;
the wisest counselors of Pharaoh give senseless counsel.
How can you say to Pharaoh,
“I am a son of the wise,
a son of ancient kings”?{h}

The princes of Zoan have become fools,
the princes of Memphis are deceived;
the cornerstones of her tribes
have led Egypt astray.{i}

For this cause my loins are full of pain;
throes have taken hold on me,
as the throes of a woman giving birth;
I am bent over from what I hear;
I am terrified at what I see.

My heart wanders, horror has overwhelmed me;
the evening twilight of my desire
he has made into a trembling for me.{c}

For thus the Lord has said to me:
“Go, set a watchman;
let him declare what he sees.

Then the lookout shouted like a lion:{f}
“Lord, I stand on the watchtower all day long,
and I am at my post every night.

O my threshed one, and son of my threshing floor,
what I have heard from Yahweh of Armies,
the God of Israel, I have declared to you.{h}

The oracle concerning Arabia.
In the thickets in Arabia you shall lodge,
O caravans of Dedanites.{j}

To the thirsty bring water;
the inhabitants of the land of Tema
met the fugitive with bread.{k}

For they have fled from the swords,
from the drawn sword,
from the bent bow,
and from the press of battle.

The oracle concerning the valley of vision.
What troubles you, then, that you are gone up,
every one of you, upon the roofs,{a}

All your leaders have run away as one;
apart from the bow they were made prisoners;
all in you who were found were bound together;
far off had they fled.{b}

Therefore I said, “Look away from me;
let me weep bitterly;
do not labor to comfort me
for the destruction of the daughter of my people.”

For it is a day of uproar, of treading down, and of bewilderment
from the Lord, Yahweh of Armies,
in the valley of vision;
a tearing down of the wall,
and a cry for help toward the mountain.{c}

And Elam took up the quiver,
with chariots of men and horsemen;
and Kir uncovered the shield.{d}

He stripped away Judah’s defenses;
and on that day you looked
to the weapons in the House of the Forest.{e}

And in that day the Lord, Yahweh of Armies,
called to weeping and to mourning,
to baldness and to girding with sackcloth;

And I will lay the key of the house of David upon his shoulder;
and he shall open, and none shall shut;
and he shall shut, and none shall open.{j}

And on many waters
the grain of Shihor, the harvest of the Nile,
was her revenue;
and she was the market of nations.{c}

Pass through your land like the Nile,
O daughter of Tarshish;
there is no restraint any more.{d}

He has stretched out his hand over the sea,
he has shaken the kingdoms;
Yahweh has given command concerning Canaan,
to destroy its strongholds.{e}

And he said, “You shall no more exult,
O oppressed virgin daughter of Sidon;
arise, pass over to Kittim;
even there you shall have no rest.”{f}

Behold the land of the Chaldeans!
This is the people that was not;
Assyria appointed it for desert creatures.
They set up their siege towers,
they stripped her palaces,
they made her a ruin.{g}

Behold, Yahweh empties the earth and makes it waste,
and twists its surface,
and scatters its inhabitants.{a}

And it shall be, as with the people, so with the priest;
as with the servant, so with his master;
as with the maid, so with her mistress;
as with the buyer, so with the seller;
as with the lender, so with the borrower;
as with the creditor, so with the debtor.

The earth mourns and withers;
the world languishes and withers;
the high ones of the people of the earth languish.

And the earth is defiled under its inhabitants,
for they have transgressed the laws,
changed the statute,
broken the everlasting covenant.{b}

In the streets there is crying over the wine;
all gladness has turned to dusk;
the joy of the land has gone into exile.

From the end of the earth we hear songs:
“Splendor for the righteous!”
But I said, “Leanness to me, leanness to me! Alas for me!
The treacherous deal treacherously;
yes, the treacherous deal very treacherously.”{f}

Broken, broken down is the land;
shattered, shattered is the land;
tottering, tottering is the land.

Reeling, the land reels like a drunkard,
and it sways to and fro like a hut;
and its transgression lies heavy upon it,
and it falls, and shall not rise again.{h}

And they shall be gathered together as prisoners in a pit,
and shall be shut up in a prison,
and after many days they shall be punished.{i}

Then the moon shall be confounded, and the sun ashamed;
for Yahweh of Armies shall reign
on Mount Zion and in Jerusalem,
and before his elders shall be glory.{j}

O Yahweh, you are my God;
I will exalt you, I will praise your name;
for you have done wonders,
counsels from long ago, faithfulness and truth.{a}

For you have made of a city a heap,
of a fortified town a ruin;
a stronghold of strangers, so that it is no city;
it shall never be rebuilt.

And he will swallow up in this mountain
the face of the covering that is cast over all peoples,
and the veil that is woven over all nations.{c}

He will destroy death forever,
and the Lord Yahweh will wipe the tears from all faces;
he will take away the shame of his people from the entire earth,
because Yahweh has spoken.{d}

On that day people will say,
“Look, this is our God;
we waited for him, and he saved us.
This is Yahweh; we waited for him;
let’s celebrate and be glad that he saves.”{e}

For on this mountain the hand of Yahweh shall rest;
and Moab shall be threshed under him,
as straw is threshed in the water of a dung heap.{f}

On that day this song will be sung in Judah:
“We have a strong city;
he makes salvation its walls and outer defenses.{a}

The mind that is stayed on you
you keep in perfect peace,
because he trusts in you.{c}

Yes, Yahweh, as your judgments unfold,
we wait for you;
the longing of our soul
is for your name and the remembrance of you.{f}

With my soul I have longed for you in the night;
yes, with my spirit within me I seek you early;
for when your judgments are in the earth,
the inhabitants of the world learn righteousness.

O Yahweh, your hand is lifted up, yet they do not see;
let them see your zeal for your people, and be ashamed;
yes, let the fire for your adversaries consume them.{g}

O Yahweh our God,
lords other than you have been masters over us;
but by you only do we make mention of your name.

They are dead, they shall not live;
they are shades, they shall not rise;
therefore you have visited and destroyed them,
and made every memory of them perish.{h}

You have enlarged the nation, Yahweh;
you have enlarged the nation and been glorified;
you have pushed out all the borders of the land.

O Yahweh, in trouble they came looking for you;
they poured forth a muttered prayer
when your chastening lay on them.{i}

We were with child, we writhed,
we have as it were given birth to wind;
we have not wrought deliverance in the land,
nor have inhabitants of the world been born.{j}

Come, my people, enter your chambers,
and shut your doors behind you;
hide yourself for a little moment,
until the indignation passes by.{l}

I, Yahweh, am its keeper;
every moment I water it;
lest any harm it,
I keep it night and day.

Or else let him take hold of my strength,
let him make peace with me;
peace let him make with me.”

In days to come Jacob shall take root;
Israel shall blossom and bud,
and fill the face of the world with fruit.

When its branches dry up, they are broken off;
women come and use them as firewood.
This is a people without understanding;
so their Maker will not pity them,
and the one who formed them will not be kind to them.

Look, the Lord has someone strong and powerful;
like a hailstorm and a destructive windstorm,
like a flood of mighty overflowing water,
he throws it down to the ground with his hand.{b}

For it is tsav latsav, tsav latsav,
