which you did not foresee.{g}

Keep on, then, with your charms,
and with the throng of your witchcrafts,
over which you have toiled since your youth;
it may be you can gain by them;
it may be you can make men tremble.{h}

You are worn out by your many advisers;
let them rise up, I pray, and rescue you,
the dividers of the sky, the watchers of the stars,
who month by month announce
the things that are coming on you.{i}

Behold, they are become like stubble;
the fire burns them;
they cannot deliver themselves
from the power of the flame.
No coal is this for warming oneself,
no fire to sit before!

That is what they will be to you, those you worked with,
those who did business with you from your youth;
they drift away, each in his own direction;
no one is left to save you.{j}

For they call themselves after the holy city,
and lean upon the God of Israel;
Yahweh of Armies is his name.

The former things I declared long ago;
out of my mouth they went, and I made them heard;
all at once I acted, and they took place.

I declared them to you from of old;
before they came about I made you hear them,
lest you should say, “It was my idol that worked them;
my graven and my molten image ordained them.”

You have heard it; now look at all of it;
will you not admit it?
From now on I am telling you new things,
hidden things that you did not know.{b}

Now they are brought into being, and not of old;
and before this day you did not hear them,
lest you should say, “Behold, I knew them.”

No, you did not hear; no, you did not know;
no, from long ago your ear was not unstopped;
for I knew how very faithlessly you would deal,
and that from the womb you were called a rebel.

For my sake, for my own sake I act;
for how could it be profaned?
And my glory to another I will not yield.{d}

Come near to me, hear this:
from the beginning I have not spoken in secret;
from the time it came to be, I was there.
And now the Lord Yahweh has sent me, and his Spirit.{g}

If only you had listened to my commands!
Your peace would then have flowed like a river,
and your righteousness like the waves of the sea;

Go out from Babylon, flee from the Chaldeans!
With a voice of singing declare it, make it heard;
send it forth to the end of the earth;
say, “Yahweh has redeemed his servant Jacob!”{i}

And they were not thirsty when he guided them through the wastelands;
water out of the rock he caused to run for them;
he cleaved the rock, and out streamed the waters.{j}

Listen to me, O coastlands,
and give heed, you peoples from far away!
Yahweh called me from the womb;
from my mother’s body he made mention of my name.{a}

And he has set my mouth as a keen sword;
he has kept me hidden in the shade of his hand;
and he has made me a burnished shaft;
he has stored me away in his quiver.{b}

But I said, “I have toiled for nothing;
for emptiness and vapor I have used up my strength;
yet surely my right is with Yahweh,
and my wage with my God.”{d}

he says, “It is a light thing for you to be my servant,
for raising the tribes of Jacob,
and for restoring the preserved of Israel;
and I will give you as a light to the Gentiles,
to be my salvation unto the farthest part of the earth.”{f}

Thus says Yahweh:
In a time of favor I have answered you,
and in a day of salvation I have helped you;
I will guard you and give you as a covenant for the people,
to restore the land,
to apportion the desolate heritages,{h}

they shall not hunger nor thirst,
neither shall scorching heat nor sun strike them;
for he who has compassion on them will lead them,
and by springs of water he will guide them.{i}

Behold, these shall come from afar,
and behold, these from the north and from the west,
and these from the land of Sinim.{j}

The children born while you were bereaved will still say within earshot,
“This place is too crowded for me;
move over so I can live here.”{m}

This is what the Lord Yahweh says:
I will raise my hand toward the nations
and lift my banner for the peoples;
they will carry your sons in their arms,
and your daughters will ride on their shoulders.{n}

Kings will be your foster fathers,
and their queens your nursing mothers;
they will bow down to you, faces to the ground,
and lick the dust off your feet.
And you will recognize that I am Yahweh;
no one who waits for me will be disappointed.

The Lord Yahweh has opened my ear,
and I was not rebellious;
I did not turn backward.

My back I offered to the smiters,
and my cheeks to them that tore out the hair;
my face I did not cover
from disgrace and spittle.{d}

But the Lord Yahweh helps me;
that is why I have not been humiliated;
that is why I have made my face hard as flint,
and I know I will not be ashamed.{e}

He who vindicates me is near.
Who will contend with me? Let us stand up together.
Who is my adversary? Let him come near to me.{f}

Behold, the Lord Yahweh helps me;
who is he who will condemn me?
Behold, all of them shall wear out like a garment;
the moth shall eat them up.

Consider Abraham your father,
and Sarah who gave you birth;
for I called him when he was one alone,
and I blessed him and made him many.{b}

For Yahweh has consoled Zion;
he has consoled all her ruined places;
he will make her desert like Eden
and her wasteland like Yahweh’s garden;
joy and gladness will be found in her,
thanks and the sound of singing.{c}

Listen carefully, my people,
and hear me, my nation;
instruction will come out from me,
and I will set my justice as a light for the peoples.{d}

My righteousness is near;
my salvation has gone forth,
and my arms shall judge the peoples;
on me the coastlands wait,
and on my arm they set their hope.{e}

Raise your eyes to the sky
and look at the ground below;
the sky will disappear like smoke,
the earth will wear out like clothing,
and its people will die like flies;
but my deliverance will last forever,
and my righteousness will never fail.{f}

For the moth shall eat them up like a garment,
and the worm shall eat them like wool;
but my righteousness shall be forever,
and my salvation to all generations.{g}

The people Yahweh has bought back will return
and come to Zion singing;
everlasting joy will be on their heads;
they will be filled with gladness and joy,
and sorrow and sighing will run off.{j}

I, I am the one who comforts you;
who are you to be afraid of a mortal who will die,
of a human being who is made like grass,{k}

Soon shall the one stooped in bonds be set loose;
he shall not die in the pit,
and his bread shall not fail.{l}

For I am Yahweh your God,
who stirs up the sea so that its waves roar;
Yahweh of Armies is his name.{m}

Rouse yourself, rouse yourself,
stand up, O Jerusalem,
you who have drunk from the hand of Yahweh
the cup of his fury;
the goblet, the cup that makes men reel,
you have drunk it and drained it.{o}

These two disasters have struck you
(who will grieve with you?):
ruin and destruction, hunger and the sword;
how can I console you?{p}

Your sons have fainted;
they lie at the head of every street
like an antelope in a net;
they are full of the wrath of Yahweh,
the rebuke of your God.{q}

and I will set it in the hand of those who grieve you,
who said to your soul,
“Lie flat, so we can walk across”;
and you made your back like the ground,
like a street for them to pass over.{s}

Wake up, wake up,
clothe yourself with your strength, O Zion;
clothe yourself with your splendid garments,
O Jerusalem, the holy city;
for the uncircumcised and the unclean
shall no longer enter into you.

Shake off the dust and get up;
sit on your throne, Jerusalem;
undo the chains from your neck,
captive daughter of Zion.{a}

Hark, your watchmen! They lift up their voice;
together they cry out for joy;
for eye to eye they shall see
the return of Yahweh to Zion.{e}

Burst out together into singing,
you ruins of Jerusalem;
for Yahweh has comforted his people;
he has redeemed Jerusalem.

Turn away, turn away, go out from there;
touch nothing unclean;
go out from her midst; keep yourselves pure,
you who carry the vessels of Yahweh.{f}

For you shall not go out in haste,
nor shall you go in flight;
for Yahweh goes before you,
and the God of Israel is your rear guard.{g}

See, my servant shall act wisely;{h}
he shall be lifted up and exalted,
and shall be very high.{i}

Just as many were appalled at you{j}—
his look was so disfigured, past that of any man,{k}
and his shape past that of mankind—

so shall he sprinkle many nations;{l}
kings shall shut their mouths because of him;
for what was not told them they shall see,
and what they had not heard they shall understand.{m}

For he grew up before him like a young shoot,{c}
and like a root out of parched ground;
he had no form nor majesty that we should look upon him,
nor any appearance that we should desire him.

He was despised and forsaken by men,{d}
a man of pains, and acquainted with sickness;{e}
and as one from whom people hide their face
he was despised, and we did not esteem him.

Surely he has borne our sicknesses,
and carried our pains;
yet we ourselves accounted him stricken,
struck down by God, and afflicted.{f}

But he was wounded for our rebellion,{g}
crushed for our guilt;
the punishment that brought us peace fell on him,{h}
and through his wounds we are healed.{i}

All of us like sheep have wandered;
each one we have turned to his own way;
and Yahweh has made to fall on him
the iniquity of us all.{j}

He was oppressed, and he humbled himself,{k}
yet he opened not his mouth;
as a lamb led to the slaughter,
and as a ewe before her shearers is dumb,
so he opened not his mouth.{l}

Through oppression and a verdict he was taken away;{m}
who among his contemporaries thought about{n}
how he was cut off from the land of the living,
struck down for the rebellion of my people?{o}

And his grave was assigned with the wicked,{p}
and with a rich man in his death,{q}
though he had committed no violence,
nor was deceit found in his mouth.{r}

Yet it was the will of Yahweh to crush him;
he made him sick.{s}
When his life makes an offering for guilt,{t}
he shall see offspring, he shall prolong his days,
and the will of Yahweh shall prosper by his hand.

After his soul’s anguish he will see light{u}
and be content;
through his knowledge{v} my righteous servant{w}
will make many people righteous,
and he will carry their guilt.

Therefore I will give him a portion among the many,{x}
and with the strong he shall share the spoil,{y}
because he poured out his soul to death
and was counted with the transgressors;{z}
yet he bore the sin of many,
and for the transgressors he intercedes.{aa}

“Sing, you childless woman who never gave birth;
break into song and shout, you who never felt labor pains!
For the children of the abandoned woman are more
than those of the woman with a husband,” says Yahweh.{a}

“Widen the place of your tent,
and let the curtains of your dwellings be stretched out; do not hold back;
make your cords long and your stakes strong.

Do not be afraid, for you will not be ashamed;
do not be dismayed, for you will not be humiliated;
you will forget the disgrace of your youth,
and no longer remember the shame of your widowhood.

For your Maker is your husband,{b}
Yahweh of Armies is his name;
and the Holy One of Israel is your Redeemer;
he is called the God of all the earth.

“O afflicted one, storm-tossed, not comforted,
see, I will set your stones in antimony,{e}
and lay your foundations with sapphires.{f}

I will make your battlements of rubies,{g}
and your gates of carbuncles,
and all your border of precious stones.

You will be established on a foundation of righteousness;
stay far from oppression, for you have nothing to fear,
and far from terror, for it will not approach you.

“Ho! All you who are thirsty, come to the waters;
and you that have no silver, come, buy grain and eat!
Yes, come, buy wine and milk
for no silver and for no price.{a}

Bend your ear and come to me;
hearken, and your soul shall live;
and I will cut for you a covenant forever,
the faithful mercies of David.{b}

Instead of the thornbush the cypress shall come up;
instead of the brier the myrtle shall come up;
and it shall be to Yahweh for a name,{d}
for an everlasting sign that shall not be cut off.”

Thus says Yahweh:
“Keep justice and do righteousness,
for near is my salvation to come,
and my righteousness to be revealed.{a}

I will give in my house and within my walls
a monument and a name{b}
better than sons and daughters;
I will give them an everlasting name
that shall not be cut off.

those I will bring to my holy mountain
and fill with joy in my house of prayer;
their burnt offerings and other sacrifices
will be accepted on my altar;{c}
for my house will be called a house of prayer
for all the peoples.”{d}

His watchmen are blind;{f}
none of them has knowledge;
they are all mute dogs;
they cannot bark;
dreaming,{g} lying down,
loving to slumber.

The dogs are greedy of soul;{h}
they never know when they have enough.
And these are shepherds
who have no understanding;
all of them have turned to their own way,
each to his own gain, to the last man.

“Come,” they say, “I will fetch wine,{i}
and let us drink our fill of strong drink;
and tomorrow shall be as today,
great beyond all measure.”

He enters into peace;
they rest upon their beds,
each one who walks straight ahead.{a}

“But you, come near here,
sons of a sorceress,
offspring of an adulterer and of one who plays the harlot.{b}

Among the smooth stones of the valley is your portion;{d}
they, they are your lot;
to them also you have poured out a drink offering,
you have brought up a grain offering.
Shall I be consoled over these things?

Behind the door and the doorpost
you have set your memorial;{e}
for, deserting me, you uncovered your bed,
you went up onto it, you made it wide;
and you made a bargain for yourself with them;
you loved their bed;
you gazed upon a hand.{f}

For I will not contend forever,
nor will I always be angry;
for then the spirit would grow faint before me,
even the breath of life that I have made.{k}

Because of his sinful greed I was angry;
I struck him, hid my face and was furious;
yet he kept on turning away,
following his own heart’s path.

I have seen his ways, and I will heal him;
I will lead him and restore comfort to him{l}
and to those who mourn for him,

I create the fruit of the lips.{m}
Peace, peace to those far away and to those near,”
says Yahweh, “and I will heal them.”{n}

But the wicked are like the tossing sea,
for it cannot be still,
and its waters cast up mire and mud.

“Cry with a full throat, do not hold back;
lift up your voice like a ram’s horn;{a}
tell my people their transgression,
and the house of Jacob their sins.

Is it not to share your bread with the hungry,
and to bring the wandering poor home with you;
that when you see one naked you clothe him,{d}
and do not turn away from your own kin?

Then your light shall burst forth like the dawn,
and your healing shall sprout up quickly;
your righteousness shall go before you;
the glory of Yahweh shall gather you in behind.{e}

For your hands are stained with blood,
and your fingers with iniquity;
your lips have spoken falsehood;{a}
your tongue murmurs wrong.

No one sues justly;
no one goes to law honestly;
they trust in emptiness, they speak lies;
they conceive trouble and give birth to iniquity.

They hatch the eggs of vipers;
they weave the spider’s web;
he that eats of their eggs dies,
and the one that is crushed bursts into an adder.

Their feet run to evil,
and they make haste to shed innocent blood;
their thoughts are thoughts of iniquity;
ruin and destruction are on their highways.{b}

The way of peace they know not,
and there is no justice in their tracks;
they have made their paths crooked for themselves;
no one who walks in them knows peace.

Therefore justice is far from us,
and righteousness does not reach us;
we wait for light, and see, darkness;
for brightness, and we walk in gloom.

We feel our way along the wall like the blind;
we grope as if we had no eyes;
we trip in broad daylight as if at dusk;
among the healthy we are like the dead.{c}

For our transgressions are many before you,
and our sins bear witness against us;
for our transgressions are with us,
and we know our iniquities:

Justice is pushed backward,
and righteousness keeps its distance;
for truth has fallen in the street,
and uprightness cannot enter.

As their deeds deserve, so shall he pay back:
fury to his foes, requital to his enemies;
to the coastlands he will render recompense.

People from the west will fear Yahweh’s name,
and those from the east his glory;
for he will arrive like a rushing river,{e}
driven by the breath of Yahweh.

Lift up your eyes round about, and see;
they all gather together, they come to you;
your sons shall come from far off,
and your daughters shall be carried on the hip.{a}

Throngs of camels shall cover you,
young camels from Midian and Ephah;
they shall all come from Sheba,
bearing gold and frankincense,
and they shall announce the praises of Yahweh.{b}

All the sheep of Kedar will be collected for you;
the rams of Nebaioth will serve you;
they will be accepted as offerings on my altar,{c}
and I will make my glorious house even more glorious.

Your gates shall stand open always;
by day and by night they shall never be closed,
that men may bring to you the wealth of the nations,
with their kings led in procession.{d}

Any nation or kingdom
that refuses to serve you will be destroyed;
such nations will be completely ruined.

For bronze I will bring in gold,
for iron I will bring in silver,
for timber, bronze,
for stones, iron;
and I will appoint peace as your overseers
and your taskmasters righteousness.

You will no longer have the sun for light by day,
or the moon to brighten the night;{f}
Yahweh will be your light forever,
and your God will be your glory.{g}

Your sun shall no more go down,
nor shall your moon withdraw;
for Yahweh shall be your everlasting light,
and the days of your mourning shall be ended.

The least one shall become a thousand,
and the smallest a mighty nation;
I am Yahweh; in its time I will hasten it.

The Spirit of the Lord Yahweh is upon me,{a}
for Yahweh has anointed me
to announce glad tidings to the lowly;
he has sent me to bandage the broken in heart,
to cry freedom for the captives,
and the opening of the prison to those who are bound;{b}

to proclaim the year of Yahweh’s favor,
and the day of vengeance of our God;{c}
to comfort all who mourn;

and to give those who grieve in Zion
a crown in place of ashes,{d}
joyful oil in place of mourning,
a robe of praise in place of a faint spirit;
they will be named oaks of righteousness,
Yahweh’s own planting, to display his glory.

They will rebuild the ancient ruins;
they will restore places devastated long ago;
they will repair the ruined cities,
wasted for many generations.

but you shall be called the priests of Yahweh;{e}
men shall speak of you as the ministers of our God;
you shall eat the wealth of the nations,
and in their glory you shall boast.{f}

Instead of your shame there shall be a double portion,
and instead of disgrace they shall shout for joy over their lot;
so in their own land they shall inherit twice over;
joy without end shall be theirs.{g}

For I, Yahweh, love justice;
I hate robbery with wrongdoing;{h}
and I will faithfully give them their recompense,
and make an everlasting covenant with them.

I will greatly rejoice in Yahweh;
my soul shall exult in my God;
for he has clothed me with the garments of salvation;
he has wrapped me in the robe of righteousness,
as a bridegroom adorns himself like a priest with a headdress,{i}
and as a bride decks herself with her jewels.

And nations shall behold your righteousness,
and every king your glory;
and a new name shall be given you,
which Yahweh’s own mouth shall designate.{a}

No longer shall you be named Forsaken,{c}
and your land shall no longer be named Desolate;{d}
but you shall be called Hephzibah,{e}
and your land Beulah;{f}
for Yahweh delights in you,
and your land shall be married.

and allow him no rest
till he sets Jerusalem firm
and makes her a renown in the land.{h}

Go through, go through the gates;
clear the way for the people;
build up, build up the highway;
clear it of stones;
lift up a banner over the peoples.{j}

Who is this coming from Edom,{a}
from Bozrah{b} with garments stained crimson,
so majestic in his clothing,
marching in his great strength?{c}
“It is I, announcing victory,
mighty to save.”

“I have trampled the winepress by myself,
and no one from the nations was with me;
I stomped on them in my anger
and crushed them in my fury;
their blood splashed on my clothes,
and I stained all my garments.{d}

I looked, but there was no helper;
I was astonished, but there was none to uphold;
so my own arm brought me salvation,
and my fury, it upheld me.

I trod down the peoples in my anger;
I made them drunk in my fury,
and I poured out their juice upon the earth.”{e}

He said, “They are certainly my people,
children who will not betray me”;
and so he became their Savior.

In all their suffering he suffered too,{f}
and the angel who served in his presence rescued them;
in his love and mercy he bought them back;
he picked them up and carried them
through all the days of long ago.

Then they remembered the days of long ago,
of Moses and his people.{h}
Where is the one who brought them up from the sea
along with the shepherds of his flock?{i}
Where is the one who placed within them
his Holy Spirit,

For you are our Father,
though Abraham does not know us,
and Israel does not acknowledge us;
you, Yahweh, are our Father;
our Redeemer from of old is your name.{j}

You come to the aid of those who gladly do right,
who remember you as they follow your ways.
But you were angry, and we sinned;
we have been in sin for a long time, so can we be saved?{d}

None calls on your name;
none stirs himself to lay hold on you;
for you have concealed your face from us,
and have melted us away by the power of our iniquities.{f}

But now, O Yahweh, you are our Father;
we are the clay, and you our potter;
and we are all the work of your hand.{g}

Your holy cities have become a wilderness;
Zion has become a wilderness,
Jerusalem a desolation.

“I was ready to be inquired of by those who asked not;
I was ready to be found by those who sought me not;
‘Behold me, behold me,’ I said
to a nation not called by my name.{a}

who sit among the tombs
and spend the night in secret places;{d}
who eat the flesh of swine,
and broth of foul things is in their vessels;

See, it stands written before me:
I will not be still unless I have paid back;
yes, I will pay back into their lap

for your sins and the sins of your ancestors together,
says Yahweh,
because they burned incense on the mountains
and insulted me on the hills;
I will pour into their laps
the full payment for their earlier deeds.”

And Sharon shall be a fold for sheep,
and the Valley of Achor a place where cattle lie down,{f}
for my people that have sought me.

I will destine you to the sword,
and you shall all kneel for the slaughter;
for I called, and you gave no answer;
I spoke, and you would not hear;
you did evil in my sight
and chose that in which I had no pleasure.”

Therefore thus says the Lord Yahweh:
“See, my servants shall eat,
but you shall be hungry;
see, my servants shall drink,
but you shall be thirsty;
see, my servants shall rejoice,
but you shall be put to shame;

Your name you shall leave behind as an oath for my chosen:
and the Lord Yahweh shall slay you;
but his servants he will call by another name,

But be glad and rejoice forever
in that which I create;
for see, I create Jerusalem a rejoicing,
and her people a gladness.

And I will exult over Jerusalem
and take joy in my people;
never again shall there be heard in her
the voice of weeping and the voice of crying.{j}

There shall be from there no more
a suckling of few days,
nor an old man who does not fill out his days;
for he who dies at a hundred years shall die a youth,
and he who falls short of a hundred shall be held accursed.{k}

They shall not build and another dwell;
they shall not plant and another eat;
for as the days of a tree shall be the days of my people,
and my chosen shall long enjoy the work of their hands.

They shall not toil in vain,
nor bear children for sudden terror;
for they are the offspring of the blessed of Yahweh,
and their descendants with them.

Wolf and lamb will feed together;
the lion will eat straw like an ox;
and the serpent’s food will be dust.
They will do no harm or damage
on all my holy mountain,” says Yahweh.{l}

Thus says Yahweh:
“The heavens are my throne,
and the earth the stool for my feet;
what manner of house would you build me,
and what manner of place for my rest?{a}

“Whoever slaughters an ox is like someone who kills a person;
whoever sacrifices a lamb is like someone who breaks a dog’s neck;
whoever presents a grain offering is like someone presenting pig’s blood;
whoever burns incense as a memorial portion is like someone who praises an idol.{b}
These people have chosen their own ways,
and their souls enjoy their detestable practices;

so I also will choose harsh treatment for them,
and bring upon them what they dread,
for I called, and none would answer;
I spoke, and they would not hear;
they did evil in my sight,
and chose that in which I had no pleasure.”

“Before she writhed in travail
she brought forth;
before the pangs could seize her
she was delivered of a boy.{c}

“Be joyful with Jerusalem, and exult over her,
all you that love her;
be glad with her in gladness,
all you that grieved for her;

so that you may suck and be filled
at the breast of her comforting;
so that you may drain it and take pleasure
in the fullness of her glory.”{d}

As one whom his mother comforts,
so will I comfort you;
you shall be comforted in Jerusalem.

When you see this, your heart will celebrate;
your bones will sprout like fresh grass;
Yahweh’s power will be seen in his servants,
and his fury in his enemies.

For Yahweh will execute judgment on all people
with fire and with his sword;
and those killed by Yahweh will be many.{e}

“And I, knowing their deeds and their thoughts,{g}
am coming to gather all the nations and the tongues,
and they shall come and behold my glory,

and I will place a sign among them.
And I will send those of them who escape to the nations,
to Tarshish, Pul, and Lud, the archers,{h}
to Tubal and Javan, to the distant coastlands
which have never heard report of me nor seen my glory;
and they shall declare my glory among the nations.

“And they shall go out and look
on the corpses of the men
who have rebelled against me;
for their worm shall not die,
and their fire shall not be quenched,
and they shall be an abhorrence to all flesh.”{j}
